5, 12.0756], [3.5, 12.25], [3.525, 12.4256], [3.55, 12.6025], [3.575, 12.7806], [3.6, 12.96], [3.625, 13.1406], [3.65, 13.3225], [3.675, 13.5056], [3.7, 13.69], [3.725, 13.8756], [3.75, 14.0625], [3.775, 14.2506], [3.8, 14.44], [3.825, 14.6306], [3.85, 14.8225], [3.875, 15.0156], [3.9, 15.21], [3.925, 15.4056], [3.95, 15.6025], [3.975, 15.8006], [4.0, 16.0]], "label": "Speed = t²"}, {"c": 1, "step": 1, "pts": [[0, 0], [1, 1], [1, 0], [0, 0]]}, {"c": 2, "step": 2, "pts": [[1, 0], [1, 1], [2, 4], [2, 0], [1, 0]]}, {"c": 3, "step": 3, "pts": [[2, 0], [2, 4], [3, 9], [3, 0], [2, 0]]}, {"c": 1, "step": 4, "pts": [[3, 0], [3, 9], [4, 16], [4, 0], [3, 0]]}], "points": [{"at": [0.7, 0.2], "label": "0.5", "step": 1}, {"at": [1.5, 1], "label": "2.5", "step": 2}, {"at": [2.5, 2.5], "label": "6.5", "step": 3}, {"at": [3.5, 5], "label": "12.5", "step": 4}, {"at": [4, 16], "label": "Total 22 m", "step": 5}], "steps": ["Strip 1, from 0 s to 1 s, is a trapezium. Its parallel sides are 0 and 1, so area = ½ × (0 + 1) × 1 = 0.5 m.", "Strip 2: sides 1 and 4, width 1. Area = ½ × (1 + 4) × 1 = 2.5 m. Running total: 3 m.", "Strip 3: sides 4 and 9, width 1. Area = ½ × (4 + 9) × 1 = 6.5 m. Running total: 9.5 m.", "Strip 4: sides 9 and 16, width 1. Area = ½ × (9 + 16) × 1 = 12.5 m. Running total: 22 m.", "The estimate of the distance is 22 m. The curve bends upwards, so each top edge lies above it. 22 m is an overestimate."]}}, {"h": "Units of gradient and area", "b": "The unit of a gradient is the **y-unit per x-unit**. Distance in km and time in hours give km/h. Speed in m/s and time in s give m/s². The unit of an area is **y-unit × x-unit**: m/s × s = m. Read the axis labels first."}], "example": {"task": "The graph shows a journey: straight from (0, 0) to (2, 24), flat to (3, 24), then straight to (5, 60). Time in hours, distance in km. Find the speed in the last part and compare it with the first.", "steps": [{"do": "Say that the speed in the last part is the gradient of the last straight section.", "why": "On a distance-time graph, gradient = speed."}, {"do": "Read the ends of that section: (3, 24) and (5, 60).", "why": "You need two points on the section itself."}, {"do": "Change in distance = 60 − 24 = 36 km.", "why": "Only the distance covered in this part counts, not the distance from the start."}, {"do": "Change in time = 5 − 3 = 2 hours.", "why": "The time taken in this part is the difference between its two times."}, {"do": "Speed = 36 ÷ 2 = 18 km/h.", "why": "Gradient = change in distance ÷ change in time. The unit is km per hour."}, {"do": "First part: 24 ÷ 2 = 12 km/h. Since 18 > 12, the last part is faster.", "why": "A steeper line means a faster speed, so the numbers match the shape."}], "answer": "The speed in the last part is 18 km/h. The first part was 12 km/h, so the last part is faster.", "fig": {"type": "graph", "x": [0, 5], "y": [0, 60], "xstep": 1, "ystep": 12, "xlabel": "Time (hours)", "ylabel": "Distance (km)", "lines": [{"pts": [[0, 0], [2, 24], [3, 24], [5, 60]], "c": 0}]}}, "selfx": {"q": "Why does the answer use 60 − 24 = 36 rather than just 60?", "o": ["The graph starts at 24 km, so 24 has to be taken off the start", "The speed must use the whole journey, so the full 60 km is needed", "The object only covered 36 km in this part, as 24 km was already done", "The rest period takes 24 km off the distance travelled"], "a": 2, "f": ["The graph starts at (0, 0), not at 24. The 24 km is where this part begins, not where the journey begins.", "The speed of one part uses only that part's change in distance. Using the whole journey would give an average speed.", "Correct. Gradient needs the change in distance over this part: 60 − 24 = 36 km.", "A rest does not remove any distance. The line is flat, so the distance stays at 24 km."]}, "faded": {"task": "The graph shows a walk home: straight from (2, 18) to (5, 0). Time is in hours, distance in km from home. Find the speed.", "given": ["Speed is the size of the gradient of this part.", "Change in distance: 0 − 18 = −18 km (getting closer to home).", "Change in time: 5 − 2 = 3 hours."], "q": "What is the next step?", "o": ["Speed = 3 ÷ 18 = 0.17 km/h, dividing time by distance", "Speed = −18 ÷ 3 = −6, so the speed is 6 km/h (speed has no minus sign)", "Speed = −18 ÷ 3 = −6 km/h, a negative speed", "Speed = 18 × 3 = 54 km/h, multiplying the two numbers"], "a": 1, "f": ["This divides the wrong way round. Speed is distance ÷ time, not time ÷ distance.", "Correct. The gradient is −6, but the minus only shows the walker is coming home. The speed is 6 km/h.", "Speed is how fast, so it is never negative. The minus on the gradient shows the direction. Drop it.", "Multiplying gives distance × time, which is not a speed. Divide change in distance by change in time."], "fig": {"type": "graph", "x": [0, 5], "y": [0, 18], "xstep": 1, "ystep": 3, "xlabel": "Time (hours)", "ylabel": "Distance from home (km)", "lines": [{"pts": [[2, 18], [5, 0]], "c": 0}]}}, "trap": "Reading a horizontal line as constant speed. On a distance-time graph it means stationary. Check the y-axis label first: gradient means speed only when the y-axis shows distance.", "recap": "Gradient is change in y ÷ change in x: speed on a distance-time graph, acceleration on a speed-time graph; area under speed-time is distance."}
{"s": "maths", "t": "A16", "kind": "method", "why": "Higher papers often ask for the tangent to a circle, which combines the circle equation, perpendicular gradients and straight-line equations in one question.", "hook": null, "chunks": [{"h": "Equation of a circle", "b": "A circle with **centre** $(0,0)$ and **radius** $r$ has equation $x^2+y^2=r^2$. So $x^2+y^2=25$ has radius $5$. A point is **on the circle** if its coordinates make the equation true: $(3,4)$ gives $9+16=25$. The number on the right is $r^2$, not $r$."}, {"h": "Tangent meets radius", "b": "The graph shows $x^2+y^2=25$. A **tangent** touches the circle at exactly one point. There it is **perpendicular** to the radius. So its gradient is the **negative reciprocal** of the radius gradient: flip the fraction, change the sign. Press Play, or drag the slider, to move P.", "fig": {"type": "graph", "anim": "frames", "ms": 250, "x": [-8, 8], "y": [-8, 8], "xstep": 2, "ystep": 2, "xlabel": "x", "ylabel": "y", "equal": true, "lines": [{"c": 0, "pts": [[5.0, 0.0], [4.9961, 0.1963], [4.9846, 0.3923], [4.9653, 0.5877], [4.9384, 0.7822], [4.9039, 0.9755], [4.8618, 1.1672], [4.8123, 1.3572], [4.7553, 1.5451], [4.691, 1.7306], [4.6194, 1.9134], [4.5407, 2.0933], [4.455, 2.27], [4.3625, 2.4431], [4.2632, 2.6125], [4.1573, 2.7779], [4.0451, 2.9389], [3.9266, 3.0955], [3.802, 3.2472], [3.6716, 3.394], [3.5355, 3.5355], [3.394, 3.6716], [3.2472, 3.802], [3.0955, 3.9266], [2.9389, 4.0451], [2.7778, 4.1574], [2.6125, 4.2632], [2.4431, 4.3625], [2.2699, 4.455], [2.0933, 4.5407], [1.9134, 4.6194], [1.7306, 4.691], [1.5451, 4.7553], [1.3572, 4.8123], [1.1672, 4.8619], [0.9754, 4.9039], [0.7822, 4.9384], [0.5877, 4.9653], [0.3923, 4.9846], [0.1963, 4.9961], [-0.0, 5.0], [-0.1963, 4.9961], [-0.3923, 4.9846], [-0.5877, 4.9653], [-0.7822, 4.9384], [-0.9755, 4.9039], [-1.1672, 4.8618], [-1.3572, 4.8123], [-1.5451, 4.7553], [-1.7306, 4.6909], [-1.9134, 4.6194], [-2.0933, 4.5407], [-2.27, 4.455], [-2.4431, 4.3625], [-2.6125, 4.26