's inside that is on A's side of the bisector.", "why": "A's side is where points are closer to A than to B. Both rules must hold."}], "answer": "The perpendicular bisector of AB passes through the midpoint of AB, 4 cm from A, at $90^\\circ$ to AB. Shade the part of the circle (radius 5 cm, centre A) that lies on A's side of the bisector. Keep all arcs.", "fig": {"type": "graph", "anim": "steps", "equal": true, "x": [-6, 10], "xstep": 2, "y": [-6, 6], "ystep": 3, "xlabel": "Distance / cm", "ylabel": "Distance / cm", "lines": [{"step": 1, "c": 0, "pts": [[0, 0], [8, 0]]}, {"step": 2, "c": 3, "pts": [[2.7015, -4.2074], [2.7539, -4.1733], [2.8058, -4.1385], [2.8574, -4.1031], [2.9084, -4.0671], [2.959, -4.0304], [3.0092, -3.9931], [3.0589, -3.9552], [3.108, -3.9166], [3.1568, -3.8775], [3.205, -3.8377], [3.2527, -3.7974], [3.2999, -3.7564], [3.3466, -3.7149], [3.3928, -3.6727], [3.4384, -3.63], [3.4835, -3.5868], [3.5281, -3.543], [3.5721, -3.4986], [3.6156, -3.4537], [3.6584, -3.4082], [3.7008, -3.3622], [3.7425, -3.3157], [3.7836, -3.2686], [3.8242, -3.2211], [3.8642, -3.173], [3.9035, -3.1245], [3.9423, -3.0754], [3.9804, -3.0259], [4.0179, -2.9759], [4.0548, -2.9255], [4.0911, -2.8746], [4.1267, -2.8232], [4.1616, -2.7714], [4.196, -2.7192], [4.2296, -2.6665], [4.2626, -2.6134], [4.295, -2.56], [4.3266, -2.5061], [4.3576, -2.4518], [4.3879, -2.3971], [4.4175, -2.3421], [4.4465, -2.2867], [4.4747, -2.2309], [4.5022, -2.1748], [4.5291, -2.1184], [4.5552, -2.0616], [4.5806, -2.0045], [4.6053, -1.9471], [4.6293, -1.8894], [4.6525, -1.8314], [4.6751, -1.7731], [4.6969, -1.7145], [4.7179, -1.6556], [4.7383, -1.5965], [4.7578, -1.5372], [4.7767, -1.4776], [4.7948, -1.4178], [4.8121, -1.3577], [4.8287, -1.2975], [4.8446, -1.237], [4.8596, -1.1764], [4.874, -1.1155], [4.8875, -1.0545], [4.9003, -0.9933], [4.9124, -0.932], [4.9236, -0.8705], [4.9341, -0.8089], [4.9439, -0.7472], [4.9528, -0.6853], [4.961, -0.6234], [4.9684, -0.5613], [4.975, -0.4992], [4.9809, -0.4369], [4.9